  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#the-head-element\r\n> Content model:\r\n> - If the document is an iframe srcdoc document or if title information is available from a higher-level protocol: Zero or more elements of metadata content, of which no more than one is a title element and no more than one is a base element.\r\n> - Otherwise: One or more elements of metadata content, of which exactly one is a title element and no more than one is a base element.\r\n\r\n↓\r\nThe above should be fixed following;\r\n> Content model:\r\n> - If the document is an iframe srcdoc document or if title information is available from a higher-level protocol: Zero or more elements of metadata content, of which no more than one is a title element and no more than one is a base element, **but with no descendant meta elements of character encoding declaration**.\r\n> - Otherwise: One or more elements of metadata content, of which exactly one is a title element, no more than one is a base element **and no more than one is a meta element of character encoding declaration**.\r\n\r\n　\r\n　\r\n\r\nRef: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#charset\r\n> ...\r\n> In addition, due to a number of restrictions on meta elements, there can only be one meta-based character encoding declaration per document.\r\n> ...\r\n> If the document is an iframe srcdoc document, the document must not have a character encoding declaration.\r\n",
